= Benjamin Butler

Benjamin Butler of Massachusetts is the most controversial figure in the **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical wing</span>** possibly in the entire <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican Party**</span>. His wartime administration of New Orleans earned him the nickname **Beast Butler** in the South and considerable admiration in the North.

- @butler_impeachment_pressure: Apply Impeachment Pressure
- @butler_labor_appeal: Appeal to Labor
- @butler_opposition_research: Dig Up Opposition Research
- @root: Return to main

@butler_impeachment_pressure
title: Apply Impeachment Pressure
subtitle: Butler uses the threat of impeachment proceedings to force compliance from hostile officials.
view-if: president = "Johnson" and year >= 1867
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; impeachment_unlocked = 1; radical_strength += 5; radical_dissent -= 4; moderate_dissent += 4; conservative_dissent += 4;

Butler begins laying the groundwork for impeachment proceedings, gathering evidence, lining up witnesses, and making very public statements about what the evidence shows. Johnson's allies scramble. The moderates are horrified. Butler is satisfied.

@butler_labor_appeal
title: Appeal to Labor
subtitle: Butler's working-class rhetoric and support for labor issues wins over Northern workers.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; workers_rep += 4; unemployed_rep += 3; immigrant_laborers_rep += 2;

Butler speaks the language of the factory floor with genuine conviction. His attacks on capital and his championing of the eight-hour day draw working men to the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican Party**</span> who might otherwise drift toward the Democrats or independent labor candidates.

@butler_opposition_research
title: Dig Up Opposition Research
subtitle: Butler investigates Democratic leaders and finds dirt to use against them.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; dem_relation -= 6; workers_dem -= 3; middle_class_dem -= 2; rural_dem -= 1; moderate_dissent += 2;

Butler sets his investigators to work on <span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democratic**</span> leaders, and as usual they find something worth using. The resulting exposés damage <span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democratic**</span> standing with key constituencies. Butler does not believe in clean fights.